# Initial Setup's ADSB page, ported from GCSViews/ConfigurationView/ConfigADSB.cs.
#
# The claim: Activate gives each ADSB_ and AVD_ parameter the vehicle holds and documents a control
# of the kind its documentation makes (ConfigADSB.cs:349-620); changing one records its value and
# writes nothing (:622-625); Write Params writes what was recorded, ENABLE names first, and says
# "Parameters successfully saved." (:179-205); Find shows only the controls whose name or
# description has the word (:21-116), and its OK keeps the word as InputBox keeps every titled
# answer, under InputBoxSearchForEnterasinglewordtosearchfor (InputBox.cs:73-84, 178-184); Refresh
# Params asks first (:212-218), and its "Show me again?" unticked is kept as
# SHOWAGAIN_Refresh_Params False at the click (Common.cs:260-270, 445-448), after which Refresh
# Params fetches without asking. The write is proved by the vehicle's echo, and put back.
#
# SITL's copter, with ADS-B and avoidance off, lists two of them: ADSB_TYPE and AVD_ENABLE, each a
# list of values. The other kinds - a RangeControl, a bitmask - and a bitmask's writes on showing
# the page again need parameters SITL lists only once ADS-B is on; the unit tests in
# crates/mp-gui/src/config/adsb.rs cover them. ADSB is the last entry under Mandatory Hardware
# (InitialSetup.cs:262-263, `mand`), not Optional Hardware.
#
# A config.xml of its own, so no "Show me again?" answer or ADSB favourite of the machine's
# Mission Planner changes the order or the question.
#
# Needs SITL copter on tcp:127.0.0.1:5760 started from tools/sitl/params/copter.parm. Run as
#
#   tools/gui-test.sh tests/gui/config-adsb.gui -- tcp:127.0.0.1:5760
#
# A run that stops half way can leave AVD_ENABLE at 1; the first expectation on it then fails
# until a fresh SITL.

env MP_CONFIG_XML $WORK/config.xml
screen params
window 1600x1200
budget 22
# RawParamWarning, on the Full Parameter List's Activate (ConfigRawParams.cs:92): "Show me
# again?" unticked, so no later visit asks, and OK.
# The vehicle first: a click before its first heartbeat is a click the screen may forget
# (vehicle.connected only says the link is open).
expect vehicle.count > 0
click raw-param-warning-again
click raw-param-warning-ok

click param-download
expect params.held > 1000

click tab-setup
expect config.adsb.active false
click setup-page-ConfigMandatory
click setup-page-ConfigADSB
expect setup.page ConfigADSB
expect config.adsb.active true

# What Activate built: two lists of values, in name order.
expect config.adsb.controls 2
expect config.adsb.order ADSB_TYPE,AVD_ENABLE
expect config.adsb.ADSB_TYPE.kind values
expect config.adsb.ADSB_TYPE.text Disabled
expect config.adsb.ADSB_TYPE.label ADSB Type (ADSB_TYPE)
expect config.adsb.AVD_ENABLE.kind values
expect config.adsb.AVD_ENABLE.text Disabled
expect config.adsb.changed 0
expect config.adsb.write none

# Choosing a value records it and writes nothing.
click adsb-AVD_ENABLE
click adsb-AVD_ENABLE-1
expect config.adsb.AVD_ENABLE.text Enabled
expect config.adsb.changed 1
expect config.adsb.changed.AVD_ENABLE 1
expect config.adsb.write none
expect params.value.AVD_ENABLE 0

# Write Params writes it, and says so.
click adsb-write
expect config.adsb.write AVD_ENABLE 1 accepted
expect params.value.AVD_ENABLE 1
expect config.adsb.message Parameters successfully saved.
expect config.adsb.changed 0
click adsb-message-ok
expect config.adsb.message none

# And back.
click adsb-AVD_ENABLE
click adsb-AVD_ENABLE-0
# Ctrl+S is ProcessCmdKey's Write Params (ConfigADSB.cs:159-168): the page took the focus when
# its list was clicked, so the chord reaches it.
key ctrl+s
expect config.adsb.write AVD_ENABLE 0 accepted
expect params.value.AVD_ENABLE 0
expect config.adsb.message Parameters successfully saved.
click adsb-message-ok

# Find: "type" is in ADSB_TYPE's name and not AVD_ENABLE's, filtered half a second after the key.
expect config.InputBoxSearchForEnterasinglewordtosearchfor none
click adsb-find
expect config.adsb.find Enter a single word to search for
type type
expect config.adsb.visible 1
expect config.adsb.ADSB_TYPE.visible true
expect config.adsb.AVD_ENABLE.visible false
expect config.InputBoxSearchForEnterasinglewordtosearchfor none
key Return
expect config.adsb.find none
expect config.adsb.search type
expect config.adsb.visible 1
expect config.InputBoxSearchForEnterasinglewordtosearchfor type
# Cancel keeps nothing new.
click adsb-find
type x
click adsb-find-cancel
expect config.adsb.find none
expect config.adsb.search type
expect config.InputBoxSearchForEnterasinglewordtosearchfor type
# Emptied, every control shows again.
click adsb-find
key ctrl+u
key Return
expect config.adsb.find none
expect config.adsb.visible 2

# Refresh Params asks first; Cancel fetches nothing.
expect config.SHOWAGAIN_Refresh_Params none
click adsb-refresh
expect config.adsb.confirm Update Params
click adsb-confirm-cancel
expect config.adsb.confirm none
expect config.adsb.refresh.enabled true
expect config.SHOWAGAIN_Refresh_Params none

# "Show me again?" unticked: kept at the click, whichever button closes the box.
click adsb-refresh
expect config.adsb.confirm Update Params
click adsb-confirm-showagain
expect config.SHOWAGAIN_Refresh_Params False
click adsb-confirm-cancel
expect config.adsb.confirm none
expect config.SHOWAGAIN_Refresh_Params False
# Refresh Params then fetches without asking. The two clicks above were answered Cancel, so
# this is the page's first fetch; over MAVFTP the list is back in well under a second, too
# quickly for the disabled button to be seen, so the count is what says a fetch happened.
expect config.adsb.refreshes 0
expect config.adsb.refresh.enabled true
expect vehicle.connected true
click adsb-refresh
expect config.adsb.press fetch
expect config.adsb.confirm none
expect config.adsb.refreshes 1
within 20
expect config.adsb.refresh.enabled true
expect params.held > 1000
expect config.adsb.order ADSB_TYPE,AVD_ENABLE

click setup-page-ConfigMandatory
expect config.adsb.active false
